  "title": "v1.0.1: Search box confused by whitespace",
  "content": "<p>If I copy the MCU part number from the <a href=\"https://www.st.com/en/evaluation-tools/nucleo-c5a3zg.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow ugc\" target=\"_blank\">NUCLEO-C5A3ZG Product Page</a></p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/880ce78c-5fc8-4fbc-a8f5-1caca6a2feb0.png\" /></figure><p> </p><p>and paste into CubeMX2, it gets a trailing space - and says “No available options”:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/419a6461-5a66-49ba-93c5-620a1887a528.png\" /></figure><p> </p><p>Removing that space does then give a list of 2 devices:</p><figure><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://uploads-eu-west-1.insided.com/stmicroelectronics-en/attachment/801ae7d1-8ec1-4d7f-bbe4-cd4ff48fcc22.png\" /></figure><p> </p><p>It really should be able to cope with trimming whitespace from the input box!</p>",
